WEBVTT

00:00:00.465 --> 00:00:43.594
Level 1 The Travels of Ibn Batuta Chapter 1 The Journey Begins My uncle, Ibn Batuta, sat by the window of his house in Tangia.

00:00:43.654 --> 00:00:50.756
It was the hot time of the day and his eyes were half open.

00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:54.816
I went into the room.

00:00:54.876 --> 00:01:00.378
Uncle, I said quietly.

00:01:00.438 --> 00:01:04.096
He looked up at me suddenly.

00:01:04.156 --> 00:01:05.584
Ah!

00:01:05.644 --> 00:01:06.365
Ah!

00:01:06.425 --> 00:01:07.255
Med!

00:01:07.315 --> 00:01:09.286
It's you again."

00:01:09.346 --> 00:01:11.457
He smiled.

00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:14.278
Yes, uncle.

00:01:14.338 --> 00:01:16.770
I answered.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:23.112
Can you tell me today about your journeys, please?

00:01:23.172 --> 00:01:28.895
I want to travel when I'm older too, I said.

00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:31.286
Is that right?

00:01:31.346 --> 00:01:33.305
He answered.

00:01:33.365 --> 00:01:37.726
Then he looked carefully at me.

00:01:37.786 --> 00:01:40.968
How old are you now?

00:01:41.028 --> 00:01:52.386
He could remember things from long ago easily, but things from the day before, not very well.

00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:57.558
I'm eleven, I said.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:04.980
Perhaps in four or five years you can begin to travel.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.341
But it's not easy, you know.

00:02:08.401 --> 00:02:18.635
You can see wonderful towns and cities, meet interesting people, and do exciting things.

00:02:18.695 --> 00:02:22.016
But there are bad times, too.

00:02:22.076 --> 00:02:30.456
You can get ill, meet big hungry animals, or lose all your money?

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:34.076
No, I said.

00:02:34.136 --> 00:02:37.827
My eyes were big and open.

00:02:37.887 --> 00:02:40.108
Yes, Ahmed.

00:02:40.168 --> 00:02:42.038
He answered.

00:02:42.098 --> 00:02:50.910
But listen to my stories, and perhaps you two can learn to come home alive.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.791
He laughed.

00:02:52.851 --> 00:02:58.198
Now, where shall I begin?

00:02:58.258 --> 00:03:03.616
I sat down, ready to listen to him.

00:03:03.676 --> 00:03:13.703
Every time my uncle told his stories, they were different, new, and interesting.

00:03:13.763 --> 00:03:18.256
I was born here in Tangier.

00:03:18.316 --> 00:03:20.088
He began.

00:03:20.148 --> 00:03:23.620
But of course, you know that.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.570
He smiled.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:32.012
My father and his father before him were judges.

00:03:32.072 --> 00:03:36.674
So I learnt to be a judge too.

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:41.506
When you're a judge, it's easy to travel.

00:03:41.566 --> 00:03:44.778
You're important, you see.

00:03:44.838 --> 00:03:48.770
Yes, I said.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:55.288
Perhaps I can be a judge too one day.

00:03:55.348 --> 00:03:58.466
He smiled.

00:03:58.526 --> 00:04:07.352
My first journey was a pilgrimage to the holy city of Makka.

00:04:07.412 --> 00:04:18.088
I got on a donkey and said goodbye to my mother and father in Tangia when I was 21.

00:04:18.147 --> 00:04:22.544
My mother cried.

00:04:22.604 --> 00:04:31.474
After Sunday's journey, I came to the town of Algiers.

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:40.442
Here I met more pilgrims, and we travelled to the city of Constantine.

00:04:40.502 --> 00:04:43.984
I met the rich ruler there.

00:04:44.044 --> 00:04:53.621
He looked at my dirty old coat, smiled, and gave a beautiful new coat to me.

00:04:53.681 --> 00:04:55.430
Why?

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.281
I asked.

00:04:57.341 --> 00:05:02.162
Good men help people when they need it.

00:05:02.222 --> 00:05:09.886
After some days, I left Constantine with the other pilgrims.

00:05:09.946 --> 00:05:14.907
We never stopped moving because we were afraid.

00:05:14.967 --> 00:05:21.776
Perhaps people could take our money from us when we slept.

00:05:21.835 --> 00:05:29.607
I was soon ill, and I wanted to go to bed and die.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:40.266
But my friends put me on my old donkey and hit the animal from behind to make it go quickly down the road.

00:05:40.326 --> 00:05:44.258
Did you want to come home then, Uncle?

00:05:44.318 --> 00:05:45.860
Of course.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.560
He smiled.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.788
But I journeyed to Tunis.

00:05:50.848 --> 00:05:54.944
A good traveler doesn't stop easily.

00:05:55.004 --> 00:06:00.336
I left Tunis in a caravan of pilgrims.

00:06:00.396 --> 00:06:06.650
They asked me, can you be the judge in our caravan?

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.952
Of course I said, yes.

00:06:10.012 --> 00:06:12.614
A caravan judge.

00:06:12.674 --> 00:06:16.325
Not bad work for a young man.

00:06:16.385 --> 00:06:22.938
When our caravan arrived in Alexandria, I was excited.

00:06:22.998 --> 00:06:27.700
I wanted to see the famous Faros there.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.012
I know, I said quickly.

00:06:32.072 --> 00:06:37.114
That's a big lighthouse from long ago.

00:06:37.174 --> 00:06:39.765
Did you go up it?

00:06:39.825 --> 00:06:41.566
No.

00:06:41.626 --> 00:06:42.987
He laughed.

00:06:43.046 --> 00:06:46.009
The Faros was in ruins.

00:06:46.069 --> 00:06:53.225
There wasn't a lot to see, but not far from Alexandria.

00:06:53.284 --> 00:06:58.499
I met a holy man, Burhan Ardeen.

00:06:58.558 --> 00:07:02.352
He could see into the future.

00:07:02.412 --> 00:07:05.354
And what did he tell me?

00:07:05.414 --> 00:07:10.584
You're going to visit India and China.

00:07:10.644 --> 00:07:17.394
And on your travels, you're going to meet many old friends.

00:07:17.453 --> 00:07:20.706
I was happy about this.

00:07:20.766 --> 00:07:25.868
I'm going to go far, I thought.

00:07:25.888 --> 00:07:30.451
And did you go to India and China in the end?

00:07:30.511 --> 00:07:33.973
Wait and see, Ahmed.

00:07:34.033 --> 00:07:36.522
Smiled my uncle.

00:07:36.582 --> 00:07:43.384
I arrived in Cairo eight months after I first left home.

00:07:43.444 --> 00:07:46.536
What a big city.

00:07:46.596 --> 00:07:49.868
And what a lot of people.

00:07:49.928 --> 00:07:56.482
And they never stop running here and there day and night.

00:07:56.542 --> 00:08:00.845
And near Cairo there are the pyramids.

00:08:00.904 --> 00:08:06.886
Big old buildings from the rulers of Egypt long ago.

00:08:06.946 --> 00:08:10.737
And were they in ruins?

00:08:10.796 --> 00:08:12.158
I asked.

00:08:12.218 --> 00:08:15.489
No, not the pyramids.

00:08:15.549 --> 00:08:17.340
He smiled.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:22.673
Next, I journeyed up the river Nile.

00:08:22.733 --> 00:08:28.796
After this, we traveled on camels through the hot desert.

00:08:28.856 --> 00:08:36.493
There were lots of hungry hyenas there, and at night we needed to be very careful.

00:08:36.553 --> 00:08:41.118
Of course, I cried excitedly.

00:08:41.178 --> 00:08:49.382
One night, a big hyena came and took everything from my bag, he said.

00:08:49.442 --> 00:08:52.873
But we soon left the desert.

00:08:52.933 --> 00:09:02.392
Then I traveled to the holy city of Jerusalem and visited the famous buildings there.

00:09:02.452 --> 00:09:06.048
Next I went to Damascus.

00:09:06.108 --> 00:09:09.259
What a beautiful city!

00:09:09.319 --> 00:09:20.022
Then I traveled to Arabia and visited Medina, and in the end I arrived in Mecca.

00:09:20.082 --> 00:09:33.749
After a year and a half it was wonderful to arrive in the city of my pilgrimage I learned from holy men there, and prayed for three weeks.

00:09:33.809 --> 00:09:38.290
And did you come back home then?

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:39.810
I asked.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.281
No.

00:09:41.341 --> 00:09:50.853
Every night I thought of the holy man, Burhaan al-Din, and of India and China.

00:09:50.913 --> 00:09:57.754
I was a true traveler now, and I didn't want to stop.

00:09:57.814 --> 00:10:04.386
So I left Makka with the ruler of Persia's caravan.

00:10:04.446 --> 00:10:12.512
When I was young, I heard many stories about the wonderful towns near there.

00:10:12.572 --> 00:10:18.156
But on my journey, I saw something very different.

00:10:18.216 --> 00:10:23.550
Years before, the Mongols came to these towns.

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:26.906
They killed a lot of people.

00:10:26.966 --> 00:10:32.004
and I saw many houses in ruins there.

00:10:32.064 --> 00:10:40.070
Perhaps the most interesting town on that journey was Wasit.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:46.675
A number of men with no money lived there in a big house.

00:10:46.735 --> 00:10:52.670
In the evening, they prayed and ate their dinner.

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:58.914
Then they sat near a big fire and told stories.

00:10:58.974 --> 00:11:04.368
Suddenly some of them walked into the fire.

00:11:04.428 --> 00:11:08.469
Then they ate the fire.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:15.794
One man put a snake's head in his mouth and ate it alive.

00:11:15.854 --> 00:11:19.448
And you saw all that.

00:11:19.508 --> 00:11:21.058
I cried.

00:11:21.118 --> 00:11:23.408
Yes.

00:11:23.469 --> 00:11:25.509
He laughed.

00:11:25.569 --> 00:11:30.710
I visited many interesting towns after that.

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:36.521
But I never saw men eat fire and snakes again.

00:11:36.581 --> 00:11:40.011
Then I went to beg that.

00:11:40.071 --> 00:11:43.182
What a wonderful city.

00:11:43.242 --> 00:11:46.353
But I was ill there.

00:11:46.412 --> 00:11:59.578
So I soon went back to I learnt from holy men and prayed there for a year and slowly I felt better.

00:11:59.638 --> 00:12:03.659
And what did you do next?

00:12:03.719 --> 00:12:05.360
I asked.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:09.822
I travelled by sea for the first time.

00:12:09.882 --> 00:12:13.773
It was my worst journey.

00:12:13.833 --> 00:12:28.194
He said, you can hear all about it tomorrow.

00:12:28.253 --> 00:13:10.526
Chapter 2 from Makka to Chagatai I arrived at my uncle's house early the next morning.

00:13:10.586 --> 00:13:18.142
So, where did you go on your first sea-journey uncle?

00:13:18.202 --> 00:13:19.803
I asked.

00:13:19.863 --> 00:13:23.026
Listen and learn.

00:13:23.086 --> 00:13:29.740
He said, and then he told me more of his story.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:37.756
After my first visit to Mucker, I wanted to see more of the world.

00:13:37.816 --> 00:13:44.230
So I traveled with friends to Jeddah, on the Red Sea coast.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:48.292
And we sailed down to Yemen.

00:13:48.352 --> 00:13:53.034
For two days, the wind was behind us.

00:13:53.094 --> 00:13:57.326
But suddenly, it changed.

00:13:57.386 --> 00:14:01.850
The sea can be dangerous, Artman.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:10.467
One minute it's beautifully quiet and the next minute it's dark and angry.

00:14:10.527 --> 00:14:22.275
The wind made our little ship go up and down in the water and I felt very ill.

00:14:22.335 --> 00:14:35.864
When we stopped at a village on the coast my friends and I got off We finished our journey to the city of Aden by camel.

00:14:35.924 --> 00:14:45.450
There, we heard stories about a number of famous places in East Africa.

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:52.946
So we got on a new ship and sailed down the African coast.

00:14:53.006 --> 00:14:58.838
Happily, I wasn't ill at all this time.

00:14:58.898 --> 00:15:10.474
After we visited different East African places, we sailed back to South Arabia some months later.

00:15:10.534 --> 00:15:18.308
Then we wanted to visit Oman, so we took a ship there.

00:15:18.368 --> 00:15:24.863
But we got off it early because we didn't like the sailors.

00:15:24.922 --> 00:15:29.182
This wasn't a good thing to do.

00:15:29.242 --> 00:15:32.831
I understood that later.

00:15:32.891 --> 00:15:41.257
My friend and I found a guide to take us on foot to Oman.

00:15:41.318 --> 00:15:46.350
I had a big bag of expensive clothes with me.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:52.175
So I gave it to the guide and he carried it.

00:15:52.235 --> 00:16:00.024
But after some time, the guide suddenly ran away with my bag.

00:16:00.084 --> 00:16:06.011
I went after him, and I put my knife near his face.

00:16:06.071 --> 00:16:07.992
That stopped him.

00:16:08.052 --> 00:16:13.934
You must always look big and angry with bad men, Ahmed.

00:16:13.994 --> 00:16:17.206
Never forget that.

00:16:17.266 --> 00:16:24.959
The guide came back, but now I watched him day and night.

00:16:25.019 --> 00:16:30.846
He wanted to kill us, I think, and take our things.

00:16:30.906 --> 00:16:36.546
After a week of walking, we arrived in Oman.

00:16:36.606 --> 00:16:44.791
We were tired, hungry and thirsty, but happy to be alive.

00:16:44.851 --> 00:16:51.966
After Oman, I journeyed to the island of Bahrain.

00:16:52.026 --> 00:16:56.428
I saw young men in little ships there.

00:16:56.488 --> 00:17:01.428
Some of them weren't any older than you, Ahmed.

00:17:01.488 --> 00:17:11.950
They stood on the ships, looked down into the sea, and then went far under the water for a very long time.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:17.752
When they came up, they had shells in their hands.

00:17:17.812 --> 00:17:22.634
They quickly opened the shells with their knives.

00:17:22.694 --> 00:17:25.019
And what was in them?

00:17:25.079 --> 00:17:33.285
wonderful pearls, the biggest and most beautiful pearls in the world.

00:17:33.345 --> 00:17:38.076
People give a lot of money for them, you know.

00:17:38.136 --> 00:17:46.288
After Bahrain, I went back to the holy city of Mecca for a year.

00:17:46.348 --> 00:17:54.174
There, I heard interesting stories about the rich ruler of India.

00:17:54.234 --> 00:18:00.610
He gave work to judges from different countries, people said.

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:06.312
So I looked at different ways to travel to India.

00:18:06.372 --> 00:18:16.384
In the end, I went across country to Syria and then sailed up to Anatolia.

00:18:16.444 --> 00:18:23.246
There are sometimes big caravans to India from there, you see.

00:18:23.306 --> 00:18:29.230
I had a very nice journey across Anatolia.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:35.215
In every village, young men took us to a house for travelers.

00:18:35.275 --> 00:18:40.779
There they gave us lots of good things to eat and drink.

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:47.485
And when we left, all the people of the village cried and said, Goodbye!

00:18:47.505 --> 00:18:53.616
I then journeyed north with some new friends.

00:18:53.676 --> 00:18:59.706
On the mountain roads, something strange happened.

00:18:59.766 --> 00:19:04.560
One afternoon, there was a lot of snow.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:11.995
And when I looked behind me, I couldn't find my way back to my friends.

00:19:12.055 --> 00:19:16.388
So I went on my horse to find help.

00:19:16.448 --> 00:19:22.534
After some time, I came to a dark little house.

00:19:22.594 --> 00:19:30.388
At the door, I spoke to an old man, but he couldn't understand me.

00:19:30.448 --> 00:19:34.130
So he called to a younger man.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:38.452
And when I saw him, I knew him.

00:19:38.512 --> 00:19:42.394
He was an old friend from home.

00:19:42.454 --> 00:19:44.874
What good luck!

00:19:44.934 --> 00:19:52.085
He helped me to find my new friends, and we stayed the night at his house.

00:19:52.145 --> 00:20:00.750
The holy man Burhan Adim was right about meeting old friends on my travels.

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:10.698
We then journeyed to the Black Sea, sailed across it and travelled to the town of Al-Kiram.

00:20:10.759 --> 00:20:14.912
This was in green, open country.

00:20:14.972 --> 00:20:19.115
People called this place the step.

00:20:19.175 --> 00:20:23.456
There, we heard something exciting.

00:20:23.516 --> 00:20:30.607
The caravan of Rula Khan Osbegh was only three days away.

00:20:30.667 --> 00:20:41.619
It was a big city with shops, mosques and places to eat in it, and it moved from place to place.

00:20:41.679 --> 00:20:53.112
I was interested to meet Khan Osbegh He sat on a big chair with his wife by a lun, near him.

00:20:53.172 --> 00:20:56.404
She had a different caravan.

00:20:56.464 --> 00:21:07.068
We traveled with his caravan, and I learnt about by a lun, the daughter of the ruler of Constantinople.

00:21:07.128 --> 00:21:16.393
She wanted to visit her home city, so Han Osbegg asked me, can you take her there?

00:21:16.453 --> 00:21:22.476
I was very happy to travel with BioLoon's caravan.

00:21:22.536 --> 00:21:29.810
After 75 days we arrived in Constantinople.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:36.343
I stayed for a month and visited all the important places there.

00:21:36.403 --> 00:21:42.196
Then I began the long journey back to the step.

00:21:42.256 --> 00:21:44.659
It was now winter.

00:21:44.719 --> 00:21:49.715
a dark and dangerous time for step travelers.

00:21:49.775 --> 00:21:58.103
So I journeyed south to the country of Chagatay and stayed with the ruler there.

00:21:58.163 --> 00:22:04.509
My uncle stopped and began to close his eyes.

00:22:04.569 --> 00:22:08.743
And did you go to India?

00:22:08.804 --> 00:22:15.862
I asked That's a story for tomorrow, Ahmed.

00:22:15.923 --> 00:22:17.673
He said.

00:22:17.733 --> 00:22:52.046
Chapter 3 from Chagatai to Calikut.

00:22:52.106 --> 00:23:10.330
When I went back the next afternoon, my uncle was happy to see me.

00:23:10.390 --> 00:23:15.034
Ah, Ahmed, you're here again.

00:23:15.094 --> 00:23:16.204
Good.

00:23:16.264 --> 00:23:21.288
He smiled, and he began his story at once.

00:23:21.348 --> 00:23:25.411
For my long winter journey to India.

00:23:25.471 --> 00:23:36.768
The ruler of Chagatai gave me a warm coat, two horses, two camels and lots of money.

00:23:36.828 --> 00:23:46.394
We traveled south to Samarkand, a city of beautiful buildings and wonderful gardens.

00:23:46.454 --> 00:24:05.419
From there, we journeyed to the Hindu Kush Mountains, Many people die in the snow in these famous mountains, so we stopped and waited for the bad weather to change.

00:24:05.479 --> 00:24:12.044
A good traveler always thinks about the weather, Ahmed.

00:24:12.104 --> 00:24:33.662
When it was better, we got up early one morning and went slowly over the cold and dangerous mountains There was lots of snow under our feet, and we needed to put down coats for our big camels to walk on.

00:24:33.722 --> 00:24:39.808
We didn't want them to stop in the snow and die of cold.

00:24:39.868 --> 00:24:47.802
We were all very happy when the Hindu Kush Mountains were behind us.

00:24:47.862 --> 00:24:55.110
After four long months, we arrived in the north of India.

00:24:55.170 --> 00:24:59.892
And there, I saw something strange.

00:24:59.952 --> 00:25:07.665
We were on the road one day when a big animal came out from the trees.

00:25:07.725 --> 00:25:18.504
It had a fat body, little legs and a very big head with a dangerous horn on it.

00:25:18.564 --> 00:25:28.415
The animal ran at my friend's horse, and it hit the horse's leg with its horn.

00:25:28.475 --> 00:25:32.757
The horse nearly died.

00:25:32.817 --> 00:25:38.380
I later learnt the name of that strange animal.

00:25:38.440 --> 00:25:42.522
It was a rhinoceros.

00:25:42.582 --> 00:25:48.370
We journeyed to the city home of the Sultan of Delhi.

00:25:48.430 --> 00:25:51.206
Muhammad Tughlugh.

00:25:51.266 --> 00:25:56.670
I knew a lot about this man before I arrived.

00:25:56.730 --> 00:26:01.233
He liked judges from different countries.

00:26:01.293 --> 00:26:10.519
You see, Ahmad, sultans often need people from other countries to help them.

00:26:10.579 --> 00:26:15.748
I soon learnt more about the sultan.

00:26:15.808 --> 00:26:24.150
It is very important to arrive in Delhi with expensive gifts for him.

00:26:24.210 --> 00:26:30.602
He then gives you back better gifts and lots of money.

00:26:30.662 --> 00:26:35.905
And in the end, you're richer than before.

00:26:35.966 --> 00:26:44.226
So I got 30 beautiful horses and three camels for the Sultan.

00:26:44.286 --> 00:26:46.552
Remember that, Ahmed.

00:26:46.612 --> 00:26:53.784
When you meet a new ruler, always arrive with gifts.

00:26:53.844 --> 00:27:00.055
When we first came to Delhi, the Sultan was away.

00:27:00.115 --> 00:27:06.867
But when he heard about me, he made me one of his judges.

00:27:06.927 --> 00:27:12.194
I was now a rich and important man.

00:27:12.254 --> 00:27:18.870
I was, of course, excited to meet him when he arrived home.

00:27:18.930 --> 00:27:29.713
His house was very big and I needed to walk through door after door to find his room.

00:27:29.773 --> 00:27:37.405
He sat there on a gold chair with soldiers all about him.

00:27:37.465 --> 00:27:41.788
He took my hand and spoke warmly to me.

00:27:41.848 --> 00:27:44.230
for some time.

00:27:44.290 --> 00:27:54.414
The next day, I went by horse with the Sultan and his soldiers through the streets of Delhi.

00:27:54.474 --> 00:27:59.726
Lots of men on elephants came after us.

00:27:59.786 --> 00:28:06.688
They left gold money on the road behind them when they went past.

00:28:06.749 --> 00:28:12.004
And people ran here and there to find it.

00:28:12.064 --> 00:28:21.593
The Sultan could write beautifully, and he could speak four different languages.

00:28:21.653 --> 00:28:25.455
But he was often angry too.

00:28:25.515 --> 00:28:34.510
Every day he asked his soldiers to kill people, sometimes for very little things.

00:28:34.570 --> 00:28:38.874
I needed to be very careful.

00:28:38.934 --> 00:28:44.198
For two years, my work went well.

00:28:44.258 --> 00:28:51.249
But then the Sultan began to have trouble with his enemies.

00:28:51.309 --> 00:28:56.260
One ruler near Delhi fought with him.

00:28:56.320 --> 00:29:02.541
And what did the Sultan do with his enemy when he found the man?

00:29:02.601 --> 00:29:09.085
Well, Sultan Muhammad had lots of elephants.

00:29:09.145 --> 00:29:16.370
And he took some of them and put big knives on their tusks.

00:29:16.430 --> 00:29:22.062
He then put his enemy in front of the elephants.

00:29:22.122 --> 00:29:26.194
The animals played with the man.

00:29:26.254 --> 00:29:33.675
They moved their knives up and down and cut his body open.

00:29:33.735 --> 00:29:43.665
He died, of course, and it was a very bad thing for us all to watch.

00:29:43.725 --> 00:29:54.147
I took a wife, a wonderful woman, to live with me in my house in Delhi.

00:29:54.207 --> 00:30:01.048
But then, my wife's father began to fight with the Sultan.

00:30:01.108 --> 00:30:03.360
This wasn't good.

00:30:03.420 --> 00:30:08.001
because people began to speak badly about me.

00:30:08.061 --> 00:30:14.312
Perhaps I was an enemy of the Sultan, too, they said.

00:30:14.372 --> 00:30:18.664
Then something worse happened.

00:30:18.724 --> 00:30:27.566
A famous holy man, Sheikh Shihab Ad-Din, lived on a hill near Delhi.

00:30:27.626 --> 00:30:31.084
I was very interested in him.

00:30:31.144 --> 00:30:35.204
and I sometimes visited his home.

00:30:35.264 --> 00:30:43.227
But Sultan Muhammad was very angry with Sheikh Shihab ad-Din.

00:30:43.287 --> 00:30:53.311
He asked the holy man to do many different things, but Sheikh Shihab always said no to him.

00:30:53.371 --> 00:31:01.334
So in the end, the Sultan's men went and killed the holy man.

00:31:01.394 --> 00:31:10.678
And when the Sultan asked about the holy man's friends, people gave my name to him.

00:31:10.738 --> 00:31:15.010
Is Sultan Muhammad going to be angry with me?

00:31:15.030 --> 00:31:19.332
I thought, what can I do?

00:31:19.392 --> 00:31:26.935
I can't run away from him because then his soldiers are going to come and kill me too.

00:31:26.955 --> 00:31:31.421
I was very afraid.

00:31:31.481 --> 00:31:36.008
I stopped eating and drank only water.

00:31:36.068 --> 00:31:44.346
In the end I left Delhi and stayed with a different holy man for five months.

00:31:44.406 --> 00:31:54.855
I gave away all my expensive things and beautiful clothes and I prayed from morning to night.

00:31:54.915 --> 00:32:05.752
Then one day The Sultan soldiers came to visit me with horses and new clothes.

00:32:05.812 --> 00:32:10.375
The Sultan wants to see you, they said.

00:32:10.436 --> 00:32:17.882
I put on my new clothes, went back to Delhi and sat before the Sultan.

00:32:17.942 --> 00:32:25.877
Ibn Batuta, you're going to be my man in China.

00:32:25.937 --> 00:32:28.158
He smiled.

00:32:28.218 --> 00:32:33.490
I have fifteen Chinese visitors here.

00:32:33.550 --> 00:32:42.044
Go back to China with them, and take gifts from me for their ruler.

00:32:42.105 --> 00:32:50.248
I couldn't say no to the Sultan, and of course I wanted to see China.

00:32:50.308 --> 00:32:58.147
But very importantly, I could now leave the Sultan and stay alive.

00:32:58.207 --> 00:33:02.514
so I said yes at once.

00:33:02.574 --> 00:33:15.419
I left Delhi in a big caravan with gifts for the ruler of China, lots of horses and big bags of gold.

00:33:15.479 --> 00:33:20.061
My wife and young daughter came with me too.

00:33:20.121 --> 00:33:25.854
We had a thousand of the Sultan's best soldiers with us.

00:33:25.914 --> 00:33:27.777
That was good.

00:33:27.837 --> 00:33:34.624
because four days later we met four thousand of the sultan's enemies.

00:33:34.684 --> 00:33:41.358
We fought and killed them all, but I soon had more trouble.

00:33:41.418 --> 00:33:49.004
One afternoon I went for a walk in the mountains far from the caravan.

00:33:49.064 --> 00:33:55.294
Suddenly, forty bandits came out from behind some rocks.

00:33:55.354 --> 00:34:02.684
They wanted to take all my expensive clothes from me, and to kill me too.

00:34:02.744 --> 00:34:12.980
Of course, I didn't want to die, so I told them lots of good stories, and I gave them all my clothes.

00:34:13.040 --> 00:34:19.025
In the morning, I was a free man, but I had nothing to wear.

00:34:19.085 --> 00:34:28.342
Only my trousers For days, I walked in the mountains with no body to help me.

00:34:28.402 --> 00:34:33.304
From time to time, I saw more bandits.

00:34:33.365 --> 00:34:39.387
But I went quickly behind rocks and trees, and they didn't see me.

00:34:39.448 --> 00:34:45.722
In the end, I was tired, cold and hungry.

00:34:45.782 --> 00:34:50.261
One day, a good traveler found me.

00:34:50.321 --> 00:34:53.650
and he carried me to the next village.

00:34:53.710 --> 00:35:04.087
I had the best dinner in the world there, and it was wonderful to put on warm clothes too.

00:35:04.147 --> 00:35:09.220
Two days later, I found the caravan again.

00:35:09.280 --> 00:35:15.274
My wife and young daughter were very happy to see me.

00:35:15.334 --> 00:35:24.735
We journeyed to the town of Cambay, and carried all our beautiful gifts onto four ships.

00:35:24.795 --> 00:35:35.046
Then we sailed south to Calicut and put everything on three big Chinese ships there.

00:35:35.106 --> 00:35:41.869
I went to the mosque that afternoon and prayed for a good journey.

00:35:41.929 --> 00:35:49.707
But before I got on the ship, something very bad happened.

00:35:49.767 --> 00:35:58.780
The weather suddenly changed and the wind broke two of our ships on rocks by the coast.

00:35:58.840 --> 00:36:02.071
We lost everything.

00:36:02.131 --> 00:36:07.022
The gifts, the people and the animals.

00:36:07.082 --> 00:36:19.337
The third ship with my wife and daughter on it sailed away, and I never saw it or them again.

00:36:19.397 --> 00:36:28.360
I needed to go back to the Sultan and tell him about all this, but I was afraid.

00:36:28.420 --> 00:36:33.621
When the Sultan was angry, he often killed people.

00:36:33.682 --> 00:36:38.173
So did you go back to Delhi uncle?

00:36:38.233 --> 00:36:39.922
I asked.

00:36:39.982 --> 00:36:42.754
You can hear about that.

00:36:42.814 --> 00:36:45.266
Tomorrow, Ahmed.

00:36:45.326 --> 00:36:56.454
He smiled.

00:36:56.514 --> 00:37:21.983
Chapter 4 from the Maldives to China.

00:37:22.043 --> 00:37:38.297
My uncle didn't answer his door at once the next day.

00:37:38.357 --> 00:37:41.272
So I waited in the street.

00:37:41.332 --> 00:37:45.122
And I thought about the Sultan of Delhi.

00:37:45.182 --> 00:37:54.764
In my head, I could see his big angry face when he heard all about those three ships.

00:37:54.824 --> 00:38:00.534
Just then, my uncle opened the door.

00:38:00.594 --> 00:38:02.455
Ah!

00:38:02.515 --> 00:38:04.445
Hello, Ahmed.

00:38:04.505 --> 00:38:07.266
Come in and sit down.

00:38:07.326 --> 00:38:08.676
He said.

00:38:08.736 --> 00:38:13.298
And then he began his story again.

00:38:13.358 --> 00:38:18.249
Of course, I couldn't go back to the Sultan.

00:38:18.309 --> 00:38:20.989
That was dangerous.

00:38:21.049 --> 00:38:26.400
I needed to leave India at once, I knew.

00:38:26.460 --> 00:38:35.996
Then, I remembered the holy man, Burhan Adim's words about visiting China.

00:38:36.056 --> 00:38:43.635
Perhaps I could go there alone, without the Sultan's help.

00:38:43.695 --> 00:38:48.600
First, I sailed to the Maldives.

00:38:48.660 --> 00:38:56.786
They are truly wonderful islands, and there are about 2,000 of them.

00:38:56.846 --> 00:39:01.790
The Maldives are famous for their beautiful shells.

00:39:01.850 --> 00:39:10.794
The people there don't have gold money, For them, shells are money.

00:39:10.854 --> 00:39:16.126
I stayed on the island of Mali.

00:39:16.187 --> 00:39:24.870
I wanted only to visit the place, but the rulers there needed a new judge.

00:39:24.930 --> 00:39:32.043
When I arrived, they brought gifts of gold and pearls to my house.

00:39:32.103 --> 00:39:37.712
It wasn't easy for me to leave the island after that.

00:39:37.772 --> 00:39:42.422
So I had new work to do.

00:39:42.482 --> 00:39:46.422
I was the judge on Marley.

00:39:46.482 --> 00:39:50.464
At first, everything went well.

00:39:50.524 --> 00:39:58.136
I took a wife from an important family that I did my usual work.

00:39:58.196 --> 00:40:02.658
But I soon began to have enemies.

00:40:02.718 --> 00:40:07.912
I was a rich man, and people didn't like that.

00:40:07.972 --> 00:40:12.034
so they said bad things about me.

00:40:12.094 --> 00:40:17.785
After nine months, it was time to sail away.

00:40:17.845 --> 00:40:26.596
My wife wasn't a good sea traveler, so I left her behind on the island.

00:40:26.656 --> 00:40:35.728
You sometimes need to leave a place quickly, Ahmed, before things go badly wrong.

00:40:35.788 --> 00:40:43.653
I left for China, But first, I sailed to the island of Serendip.

00:40:43.713 --> 00:40:53.655
When we were nine days away from it, we could see its famous mountain, Adams Mountain, across the sea.

00:40:53.715 --> 00:41:07.138
Many people make the pilgrimage to this holy mountain, because on it, you can see a footprint of Adam, the first man in our world.

00:41:07.198 --> 00:41:13.110
I stayed with the Sultan of Serendib for three days.

00:41:13.170 --> 00:41:22.406
He loved listening to my traveler's stories, and he gave me pearls and big rubies.

00:41:22.466 --> 00:41:26.938
Serendib is famous for its rubies, you see.

00:41:26.998 --> 00:41:33.236
The women there wear them all over their arms and legs.

00:41:33.296 --> 00:41:38.994
The Sultan told me all about Adam's mountain.

00:41:39.054 --> 00:41:48.310
There are two ways to walk up to Adam's footprint, an easy way and a dangerous way.

00:41:48.370 --> 00:41:54.332
You're a true pilgrim only when you go the dangerous way.

00:41:54.393 --> 00:41:59.194
So, of course, I went up that way.

00:41:59.254 --> 00:42:06.146
It was a long journey over big rocks and between dark trees.

00:42:06.206 --> 00:42:11.050
But we arrived in the end at Adam's footprint.

00:42:11.110 --> 00:42:14.102
It was wonderful there.

00:42:14.163 --> 00:42:21.248
You're up in the sky and you can see things very far away.

00:42:21.308 --> 00:42:27.761
After that, I left Serendibh by ship for India.

00:42:27.822 --> 00:42:34.274
I was a happy man, with lots of pearls and rubies in my bag.

00:42:34.334 --> 00:42:38.798
But soon things went wrong.

00:42:38.858 --> 00:42:44.772
One day, sudden winds took our ship onto some rocks.

00:42:44.832 --> 00:42:49.106
I was afraid, because I can't swim.

00:42:49.166 --> 00:42:58.047
The sailors took some of the women travellers away, but I stayed alone all night on the ship.

00:42:58.108 --> 00:43:00.385
and prayed.

00:43:00.445 --> 00:43:08.552
In the morning some people found me and took me back to the coast of Cenindib.

00:43:08.612 --> 00:43:16.668
I sailed away once more, but this time lots of pirates came onto our ship.

00:43:16.728 --> 00:43:27.562
They took all my pearls, rubies and expensive clothes, and then left me on an island in only my trousers.

00:43:27.622 --> 00:43:31.054
Not again, I thought.

00:43:31.114 --> 00:43:40.690
I sailed back to the Maldives once more, and there I got on a ship to China.

00:43:40.750 --> 00:43:46.005
On the journey, I stopped at a number of places.

00:43:46.066 --> 00:43:52.322
and visited two islands, Sumatra and Java.

00:43:52.382 --> 00:43:56.126
Java was very interesting.

00:43:56.186 --> 00:44:03.272
Everybody there has an elephant and people visit the shops on them.

00:44:03.332 --> 00:44:12.760
After Java, we sailed for 40 days with a good wind behind us and arrived in China.

00:44:12.820 --> 00:44:17.454
There's a lot to tell you about China, Ahmed.

00:44:17.514 --> 00:44:27.982
Chinese people can make many different things very well, from wonderful pictures to beautiful boxes.

00:44:28.042 --> 00:44:37.728
China is a very nice country for travelers, and I journeyed easily from town to town.

00:44:37.788 --> 00:44:43.170
Some of their animals are different from our animals, too.

00:44:43.230 --> 00:44:45.838
And that interested me.

00:44:45.898 --> 00:44:51.648
They have cats with blue-green eyes, you know.

00:44:51.708 --> 00:45:00.120
And when I stopped in one city called Fuzhu, something very interesting happened.

00:45:00.180 --> 00:45:06.611
A judge arrived in the city, and my friends took me to meet him.

00:45:06.671 --> 00:45:08.921
We said, hello.

00:45:08.981 --> 00:45:13.777
And then this man looked at me, and I looked at him.

00:45:13.837 --> 00:45:17.394
I know you," I cried.

00:45:17.454 --> 00:45:22.127
You're Al Buschry, and you're from Seuta.

00:45:22.187 --> 00:45:26.050
Not far from my hometown of Tangier.

00:45:26.110 --> 00:45:29.892
That's right, he smiled.

00:45:29.953 --> 00:45:33.926
We laughed and talked for hours.

00:45:33.986 --> 00:45:38.984
You meet people in the strangest places, Ahmed.

00:45:39.044 --> 00:45:48.405
The holy man, Burhan Adim, was right again about finding old friends on my journeys.

00:45:48.465 --> 00:45:56.490
After some months in China, I was ready to begin my long journey home.

00:45:56.550 --> 00:46:00.592
So I went to look for a ship.

00:46:00.652 --> 00:46:05.916
And did you come home at once, I asked?

00:46:05.976 --> 00:46:08.815
No, he said.

00:46:08.875 --> 00:46:17.222
I stopped at cities from my earlier journeys, Damascus, Cairo, and many more.

00:46:17.283 --> 00:46:23.610
But when I went back, they were dark and different places.

00:46:23.670 --> 00:46:39.364
He said slowly, I can tell you all about that tomorrow.

00:46:39.424 --> 00:47:20.717
Chapter 5 to Tangia and Granada So, what was the trouble with those cities when you visited them again?

00:47:20.777 --> 00:47:24.828
I asked my uncle when I arrived the next day.

00:47:24.888 --> 00:47:29.659
Let's talk about my journey from China first.

00:47:29.719 --> 00:47:32.299
He answered quietly.

00:47:32.359 --> 00:47:38.600
On my way back from China, I stopped in Sumatra again.

00:47:38.660 --> 00:47:42.327
Then I got on a big ship.

00:47:42.387 --> 00:47:46.806
and sailed for 40 days to India.

00:47:46.866 --> 00:47:55.784
When I arrived there, I thought about visiting the Sultan, but I was afraid.

00:47:55.844 --> 00:48:03.800
Perhaps he remembered his gifts for the ruler of China and the time when I lost them all.

00:48:03.860 --> 00:48:15.144
From India, I sailed to the south coast of Arabia, I then traveled through Persia to Baghdad.

00:48:15.204 --> 00:48:24.467
I journeyed across the desert, and in the end, I arrived once more in the city of Damascus.

00:48:24.527 --> 00:48:32.960
It was twenty years from the time of my last visit, but I remembered it well.

00:48:33.020 --> 00:48:38.540
In Damascus, I heard something interesting.

00:48:38.600 --> 00:48:44.932
A teacher from Tangier now lived and worked in the city.

00:48:44.992 --> 00:48:53.328
I was excited to meet this man, and I asked him at once for news from home.

00:48:53.388 --> 00:49:00.424
My father was dead, but my mother was alive, he told me.

00:49:00.484 --> 00:49:15.276
I felt bad about my father, and suddenly, after 24 long years away, I began to think of going back home and of seeing my mother.

00:49:15.336 --> 00:49:22.458
I journeyed to Aleppo, but there I heard some bad news.

00:49:22.518 --> 00:49:28.939
The plague wasn't far away and many people were ill with it.

00:49:28.999 --> 00:49:35.848
At first I travelled quickly from city to city in Syria.

00:49:35.908 --> 00:49:40.388
I wanted to stay in front of the plague, you see.

00:49:40.448 --> 00:49:50.518
But after a time, when I arrived in new places, the plague was there before me.

00:49:50.578 --> 00:49:55.173
So I went back to Damascus.

00:49:55.233 --> 00:49:59.000
Here I learnt the worst.

00:49:59.060 --> 00:50:07.456
At that time, lots of men, women, and children died of plague there every day.

00:50:07.516 --> 00:50:18.770
Everybody came out into the streets with their holy books and prayed for their families, but nobody could stop the plague.

00:50:18.830 --> 00:50:24.372
The news of the plague made me think of my mother again.

00:50:24.392 --> 00:50:29.318
Was she ill too, perhaps?

00:50:29.379 --> 00:50:39.740
So I traveled on pilgrimage to Makka one more time, and then began my way back home through Cairo.

00:50:39.800 --> 00:50:48.617
Of course, I knew this wonderful city from years before, but it was very different now.

00:50:48.637 --> 00:50:57.253
21,000 people died from the plague there every day.

00:50:57.313 --> 00:51:00.197
My uncle stopped.

00:51:00.258 --> 00:51:03.302
and looked out of the window.

00:51:03.362 --> 00:51:06.654
Did you get ill, Uncle?

00:51:06.714 --> 00:51:08.236
I asked.

00:51:08.296 --> 00:51:09.796
No.

00:51:09.856 --> 00:51:11.508
I didn't.

00:51:11.569 --> 00:51:13.900
He said slowly.

00:51:13.960 --> 00:51:17.893
And I thank God for that.

00:51:17.953 --> 00:51:27.610
I left Cairo, traveled to Tunis, and then got on a ship to the island of Sardinia.

00:51:27.670 --> 00:51:30.536
We didn't stay there long.

00:51:30.596 --> 00:51:36.802
There were bandits on the island, and they wanted to fight and kill us.

00:51:36.862 --> 00:51:39.732
So we left quickly.

00:51:39.792 --> 00:51:49.404
After Sardinia, I sailed to North Africa, and then traveled by donkey to Tangier.

00:51:49.464 --> 00:51:57.238
But not long before I arrived home, I heard bad news about my mother.

00:51:57.298 --> 00:52:02.974
She was dead, people in the town of Taza told me.

00:52:03.034 --> 00:52:07.067
I was very sorry to hear this.

00:52:07.127 --> 00:52:19.356
In the end, I went to the most important city in our country, Fez, and I met our ruler, Sultan Abu Inan there.

00:52:19.416 --> 00:52:25.714
To me, he was more wonderful than all the rulers in the world.

00:52:25.774 --> 00:52:32.664
Sometimes, Ahmed, the things in your home country are the best.

00:52:32.724 --> 00:52:40.591
After that, I went back to Tangier and visited my mother's grave.

00:52:40.651 --> 00:52:43.853
I was ill for three months.

00:52:43.914 --> 00:52:54.014
But then, I heard my friends talk about trouble in the kingdom of Granada, Al-Andalus.

00:52:54.074 --> 00:53:02.024
King Alfonso of Castile is going to fight our brothers there.

00:53:02.084 --> 00:53:06.837
They said, we must help them.

00:53:06.897 --> 00:53:13.423
Soon after that, we sailed to the kingdom of Granada.

00:53:13.483 --> 00:53:22.429
But King Alfonso died of the plague before we arrived, and we didn't need to fight.

00:53:22.490 --> 00:53:29.714
So I stayed and visited all the interesting places in that country.

00:53:29.774 --> 00:53:35.868
Now, I must tell you a story about my time there.

00:53:35.928 --> 00:53:45.474
One day, I was on the coast road to Malaga when I met 12 soldiers on horses.

00:53:45.534 --> 00:53:52.788
They asked me to journey with them because the road to Malaga was dangerous.

00:53:52.848 --> 00:53:56.730
There were enemy ships near the coast.

00:53:56.790 --> 00:54:05.743
I wanted to go with them, but in the end, I stayed behind and traveled with my friends.

00:54:05.804 --> 00:54:13.716
Later, on the road to Malaga, we found a dead horse in our way.

00:54:13.776 --> 00:54:21.905
It was one of the twelve soldiers' horses, and I soon learned their story.

00:54:21.965 --> 00:54:31.972
Those soldiers were now in the hands of dangerous enemy sailors, but I was free.

00:54:32.032 --> 00:54:39.174
I thanked God for that, and I prayed for all of our brothers.

00:54:39.234 --> 00:54:46.005
Then I journeyed to the famous city of Granada.

00:54:46.066 --> 00:54:51.947
In one of the beautiful gardens there, I met some writers.

00:54:52.008 --> 00:55:05.334
they were interested in my traveller's stories, and one young man, Ibn Juzayi, listened carefully and began to write about my long journey.

00:55:05.394 --> 00:55:15.010
I didn't know it at the time, but Ibn Juzayi was later a very important friend to me.

00:55:15.070 --> 00:55:23.406
Soon after that, I left the Kingdom of Granada and sailed back to Morocco.

00:55:23.466 --> 00:55:29.162
And this time you stayed at home in our country.

00:55:29.222 --> 00:55:31.685
Is that right, Uncle?"

00:55:31.745 --> 00:55:33.446
I said.

00:55:33.506 --> 00:55:36.719
Well, no.

00:55:36.780 --> 00:55:38.261
He smiled.

00:55:38.321 --> 00:55:39.832
I didn't.

00:55:39.892 --> 00:55:43.906
There was one more country to visit.

00:55:43.966 --> 00:55:49.888
A place of hot deserts and dangerous snakes.

00:55:49.948 --> 00:56:04.879
Come back to hear about that tomorrow morning, Ahmed.

00:56:04.939 --> 00:56:50.735
Chapter 6 Tomali and Back When I arrived the next day, my uncle said, Ahmed, you wanted to be a traveler before?

00:56:50.795 --> 00:56:54.015
Do you want to be a traveler now?

00:56:54.075 --> 00:56:58.096
Yes, I answered.

00:56:58.156 --> 00:57:04.997
It's not easy, I know, but I truly want to travel.

00:57:05.057 --> 00:57:07.898
Good, he said.

00:57:07.958 --> 00:57:10.172
So listen carefully.

00:57:10.232 --> 00:57:13.577
because there's more to learn.

00:57:13.637 --> 00:57:22.984
For my last journey, I traveled south because I wanted to visit Mali.

00:57:23.044 --> 00:57:48.593
You see, years before in Cairo, I heard many stories about the famous king of Mali, Mansa Suleiman, and all his gold, And so I left Fez and journeyed across the Atlas Mountains to the town of Sigil Masa.

00:57:48.653 --> 00:57:56.016
Now, do you remember I met a man called Al-Bushri in China?

00:57:56.076 --> 00:58:02.690
Well, in Sigil Masa I met Al-Bushri's brother.

00:58:02.750 --> 00:58:05.040
It was strange.

00:58:05.100 --> 00:58:09.480
The two brothers were in very different places.

00:58:09.540 --> 00:58:14.372
but I met the older one and the younger one.

00:58:14.432 --> 00:58:21.717
Then I traveled by camel with a caravan to Terraza.

00:58:21.778 --> 00:58:28.052
It wasn't a beautiful village, but it had some interesting buildings.

00:58:28.112 --> 00:58:36.100
The people there take big pieces of salt from the desert and make houses with them.

00:58:36.160 --> 00:58:40.202
There's a salt mosque there too.

00:58:40.263 --> 00:58:45.384
I stayed in a little salt house in the village.

00:58:45.444 --> 00:58:49.835
But the water there was very bad to drink.

00:58:49.895 --> 00:59:01.047
So after ten days we left and began our long and dangerous journey south across the hot desert.

00:59:01.108 --> 00:59:11.068
At first a friend and I left our caravan every morning to look for things to eat for our camels.

00:59:11.128 --> 00:59:16.197
But one day, we heard some bad news.

00:59:16.258 --> 00:59:26.174
Ibn Ziri, a man from our caravan, walked alone into the desert with no water bottle.

00:59:26.234 --> 00:59:31.816
Later, friends found him dead under a tree.

00:59:31.877 --> 00:59:37.060
After that, we always stayed with the caravan.

00:59:37.120 --> 00:59:41.517
You must never go alone into the desert.

00:59:41.577 --> 00:59:49.377
you can easily forget your way and die quickly in the hot sun.

00:59:49.437 --> 00:59:59.794
There were lots of big snakes in this desert too, and one man in the caravan liked playing with them.

00:59:59.854 --> 01:00:02.096
What happened to him?

01:00:02.156 --> 01:00:09.521
A snake put its teeth into one of his fingers one morning, and he nearly died.

01:00:09.581 --> 01:00:17.878
In the end, with a knife, he cut this finger from his hand, and so he lived.

01:00:17.938 --> 01:00:24.883
Remember, playing with snakes is very dangerous.

01:00:24.943 --> 01:00:34.911
We journeyed for many weeks to the biggest city in Mali, to meet King Mansa Suleiman.

01:00:34.971 --> 01:00:40.251
But soon after we arrived, I ate something bad.

01:00:40.311 --> 01:00:43.730
and I was ill for a long time.

01:00:43.790 --> 01:00:54.258
Usually, when you're an important traveler, the ruler takes expensive gifts to you when you first arrive in a town.

01:00:54.319 --> 01:01:03.606
So I waited in my bed day after day for Mansa Suleiman's men to visit me.

01:01:03.666 --> 01:01:09.304
After some weeks, the king's men arrived with gifts.

01:01:09.364 --> 01:01:16.062
Perhaps it was some nice clothes or some pieces of gold, I thought.

01:01:16.122 --> 01:01:23.136
But no, they gave me some old bread and meat.

01:01:23.196 --> 01:01:30.678
When I felt better, I visited the king's beautiful house every day.

01:01:30.738 --> 01:01:35.942
I waited for more gifts, but I got nothing.

01:01:36.002 --> 01:01:40.483
In the end, I spoke to the king.

01:01:40.543 --> 01:01:43.505
I'm a world traveler.

01:01:43.565 --> 01:01:49.950
In every country, rulers give me wonderful gifts when I arrive.

01:01:50.010 --> 01:01:54.264
I arrived in your city four months ago.

01:01:54.324 --> 01:01:56.757
But you do not speak to me.

01:01:56.817 --> 01:01:59.280
Or give me nice things.

01:01:59.340 --> 01:02:03.884
What can I say about you to other people?

01:02:03.944 --> 01:02:08.502
Things soon changed after that.

01:02:08.562 --> 01:02:18.566
Mansa Suleiman was now very good to me, and he gave me a house and a lot of gold.

01:02:18.626 --> 01:02:27.814
And when I left the city with a friend to visit the country, his men brought me more gold.

01:02:27.874 --> 01:02:34.103
In the end, my friend and I came to a big river.

01:02:34.163 --> 01:02:46.746
I saw some very strange animals in the water there, horses with big fat bodies, little legs and elephants feet.

01:02:46.806 --> 01:02:55.143
My friend called them hippopotamuses, but they were new to me.

01:02:55.203 --> 01:03:05.976
I traveled north to Timbuktu, But in a town near Timbuktu, I was very ill once more.

01:03:06.036 --> 01:03:12.159
Then one day I got a letter from the Sultan of Morocco.

01:03:12.220 --> 01:03:15.132
He needed me at once.

01:03:15.192 --> 01:03:17.083
What does he want?

01:03:17.143 --> 01:03:18.554
I thought.

01:03:18.614 --> 01:03:34.230
We traveled north for a long time and went back over the Atlas Mountains The winter snow there made the roads very dangerous, and we journeyed slowly.

01:03:34.290 --> 01:03:42.974
In the end, after some months, I arrived back at the Sultan's home in Fez.

01:03:43.034 --> 01:03:49.626
I have important work for you, he said, when he saw me.

01:03:49.686 --> 01:03:53.180
There's a young writer here.

01:03:53.240 --> 01:04:02.025
His name is Ibn Juzai, and he wants to write down all your stories.

01:04:02.086 --> 01:04:06.947
Then everybody can learn about them.

01:04:07.007 --> 01:04:12.949
Ibn Juzai, I said at once, I know him.

01:04:13.009 --> 01:04:15.870
I met him in Granada.

01:04:15.930 --> 01:04:28.592
A holy man once told me about meeting friends in different places, It happened before, and now it's happening again.

01:04:28.652 --> 01:04:34.585
Of course, it was wonderful to speak to Ibn Jusai again.

01:04:34.605 --> 01:04:46.643
I told him all about the exciting places, the different animals, and the interesting people from all my journeys.

01:04:46.703 --> 01:04:53.526
And now, Ahmed, all these stories are in a book.

01:04:53.586 --> 01:04:59.940
I'm not going to be here always, but take this.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.952
It's my gift to you.

01:05:03.013 --> 01:05:09.959
You can read it and learn more about my travels when you want.

01:05:10.019 --> 01:05:17.376
With that, my uncle put a big book into my hand.

01:05:17.436 --> 01:05:22.384
Thank you, uncle, I said.

01:05:22.444 --> 01:05:27.029
I took the book home with me that afternoon.

01:05:27.090 --> 01:05:55.505
My uncle died not long after that, but I have his book and I often read it to this day.

01:05:55.565 --> 01:07:03.908
That's it.

01:07:03.968 --> 01:08:25.687
The End.

01:08:25.747 --> 01:08:55.598
You

